   "heading": "Tables for presentation",
   "segment_index": "S1.P2",
   "kind": "untrue",
   "en_span": "chapters/tables_presentation.qmd:105-105",
   "tr_span": "chapters/tables_presentation.fr.qmd:103-103",
   "proposition": "The French says the page shows how to summarise the data of a table or a file (\"synthetiser les donnees d'un tableau ou d'un fichier\") into presentation-ready tables with flextable; the English says the page converts data frames that are ALREADY summaries into presentation-ready tables, and the very next paragraph states that the summarising must be done before flextable is used.",
   "reader_consequence": "A French reader expects flextable to perform the aggregation step, so they may pass a raw linelist to flextable() and look for summarising arguments that do not exist, instead of building the summary data frame first with dplyr/janitor as the chapter requires.",
   "confidence": "medium"
  },
  {
   "heading": "Prepare table",
